                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7b9d342-c4da-31dd-842e-b73468b42481",
                        "entry_id": "8830109f-6b0c-33f3-85d8-208d7cd24bda",
                        "glosses": [
                            "спорт. игровой вид спорта, в котором два игрока (или две пары) с помощью ракеток пытаются добиться того, чтобы целлулоидный шарик ударился последний раз о половину стола противника чаще, чем о свою"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8977d6e3-6213-4aef-a534-06dbc1a1dd96",
                                "sense_id": "e7b9d342-c4da-31dd-842e-b73468b42481",
                                "text": "Во всех НИИ Советского Союза играли в пинг-понг в обеденный перерыв и по вечерам."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0a178332-0253-4217-8719-eeabdabd8ece",
                        "source_entry_id": "8830109f-6b0c-33f3-85d8-208d7cd24bda",
                        "source_sense_id": "e7b9d342-c4da-31dd-842e-b73468b42481",
                        "target_lang_word": "ping pong",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ping pong",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b841135-c2f3-391c-88e9-1a726f8a94e8",
                                        "entry_id": "1c603ab2-d0f2-3ca6-85df-0ea3d485ebb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Table tennis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "744f8419-d5f8-469f-a7a8-a5d342cd8b9d",
                                                "sense_id": "3b841135-c2f3-391c-88e9-1a726f8a94e8",
                                                "text": "Our correspondent seems to hope that the unclean, playing Ping-Pong with the clean, will become unpleasantly conscious of his uncleanness and reform."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1adafb1a-027e-38e4-b9c0-1ddb4d5210c9",
                                        "entry_id": "1c603ab2-d0f2-3ca6-85df-0ea3d485ebb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of figuratively bouncing something or someone back and forth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c15c83c-a9dd-4693-a4e5-6880633c82a4",
                                                "sense_id": "1adafb1a-027e-38e4-b9c0-1ddb4d5210c9",
                                                "text": "To be conscious is to be subject to just such a ping-pong of recurring nervous activities that effect muscle tone on one side and brain discharge on the other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c9544b5-76da-3993-9d7b-7a46149a6d5e",
                                        "entry_id": "1c603ab2-d0f2-3ca6-85df-0ea3d485ebb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The exchange of proposed amendments between the House of Commons and House of Lords, particularly at the end of a session when compromises have to be made to complete the legislative process within the limited time available."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38f78b92-4083-3005-b533-9cd0167954d2",
                                        "entry_id": "1c603ab2-d0f2-3ca6-85df-0ea3d485ebb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A size of photograph a little larger than a postage stamp."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "dated",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ff42c2f-a348-4829-ba3a-6be15ec49690",
                                                "sense_id": "38f78b92-4083-3005-b533-9cd0167954d2",
                                                "text": "As only bust or half-length figures are all the ping pong photographer attempts, only one or two small plain backgrounds is all that is necessary. Generally two are used, a light one and a dark one."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "779fdccc-d83f-3831-8d9b-a6cba0f05f55",
                                        "entry_id": "1c603ab2-d0f2-3ca6-85df-0ea3d485ebb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small, shallow steelpan drum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82f69374-e47f-44e8-af06-8b1d78e9f772",
                                                "sense_id": "779fdccc-d83f-3831-8d9b-a6cba0f05f55",
                                                "text": "Most ping pongs were 35- to 45-gallon drums. The larger drum had room for more notes; the tones were also louder and clearer and could be sustained longer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
